  "ingredients": [
    "32 ounce london broil roast",
    "2 tablespoon soy sauce (or coconut aminos)",
    "2 tablespoon low-carb ketchup",
    "1 tablespoon dijon mustard",
    "2 teaspoon fresh garlic (minced)",
    "2 teaspoon onion powder",
    "1/2 cup chicken broth",
    "1/2 cup brewed coffee",
    "1/4 cup dry white wine"
  ],
  "instructions": [
    {
      "text": "Add the London broil to the slow cooker. Coat one side with 1/2 (of each) of the soy sauce, ketchup, dijon, and minced garlic. Turn and repeat on other side.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/london-broil-falling/#wprm-recipe-50913-step-0-0",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/02/IMG_3196.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Sprinkle onion powder over the side that is facing up.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/london-broil-falling/#wprm-recipe-50913-step-0-1",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/02/IMG_3202.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Pour chicken broth, coffee, and white wine over the meat.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/london-broil-falling/#wprm-recipe-50913-step-0-2",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/02/IMG_3204.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Set slow cooker to high and let this cook for 4-6 hours.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/london-broil-falling/#wprm-recipe-50913-step-0-3",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/02/IMG_3206.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "When meat is done, you can optionally leave the top off for a little bit to allow the liquid to reduce some more. Keep in mind that if you do this, the meat will dry out a little. Alternatively, you can remove meat and keep warm by wrapping with foil while reducing liquid.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/london-broil-falling/#wprm-recipe-50913-step-0-4",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/02/IMG_3309.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Using 2 forks, shred the meat. (If meat was removed to reduce sauce, return to pan)",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/london-broil-falling/#wprm-recipe-50913-step-0-5",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/02/IMG_3312.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Serve – I garnished with hot sauce because I love spicy! I also served them with Roasted Pecan Green Beans – delicious!",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/london-broil-falling/#wprm-recipe-50913-step-0-6",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/02/LondonBroil2.jpg"
    }
  ],
